{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/Key\/Diatonic\/diatonicCollection","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"diatonicCollection","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"PitchClass","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10PitchClassV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchClass"},{"text":"] { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The collection runs from one fifth below the major tonic to five fifths above it (for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flat: B♭ F C G D A E). A mode is an index into it: lydian 0, major 1, mixolydian 2,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dorian 3, minor 4, phrygian 5 and locrian 6.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/key\/diatonic\/diatoniccollection"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The seven pitch classes of this key’s signature, in order of ascending fifths.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning3KeyO8DiatonicV18diatonicCollectionSayAA10PitchClassVGvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","title":"diatonicCollection","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"diatonicCollection","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"PitchClass","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10PitchClassV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuni